      "writtenOn": "2022-04-18T17:06:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see your point about readability, especially the escaping part.\n\nI was wondering if in this case the type of `reg` is expected to be always the same. One advantage of the MACRO is that it works for multiple data types.\n\nIf in this context `reg` is always going to be a `uint32_t` then it shouldn\u0027t make a difference. However, if we need to handle multiple types (e.g. `uint16_t` and `uint64_t`) then I suspect we will need multiple functions, each one with its own tests.",
